      "content": "I'm so sorry you're feeling this way; discovering a fundamental failure in years of work is incredibly devastating, but it doesn't mean your talent or potential were wasted. Your advisor and lab mates likely see your resilience and shared challenges, not just the error; many breakthroughs have arisen from such critical moments where teams had to adapt and rebuild rigorously. Everyone I know in my science career has hit a wall like this and found ways to pivot, because the most valuable data is often just the problem itself. Please reach out for support if this feeling of fraud is overwhelming, and take a moment to breathe before making any major decisions today.",
