      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes complete sense that the revelation of your own faulty logic would shatter your confidence, as it feels as if there is no more foundation for you to stand on. However, remember that relying on flawed assumptions for years is a past failure, not a judgment on your actual ability as a scientist or human being. Perhaps the world will surprise you with their judgment of the science over the fallibility of its creator, and if not, you could even redo your work from a fresh start. If the shame feels too heavy to carry alone, consider speaking with a counselor who specializes in academic stress or a trusted mentor outside your immediate lab group.",
